   "body": "*Key: ★ = lecture audio add-ons · plain bullets = study guide, word for word*\n\n### LECTURE\n- ★ Contents of the true pelvis (rectum, urinary bladder, vessels) · what forms the anterior, posterior and lateral walls.\n- ★ Levator ani vs coccygeal muscles — puborectalis is levator ani only; ischiococcygeus is coccygeal only.\n- ★ What passes above and below the piriformis (greater sciatic foramen) + the lesser sciatic foramen · lumbosacral plexus: roots, divisions, obturator (anterior) vs femoral (posterior), sciatic split.\n- ★ Pelvic inlet / outlet: boundaries; sacrotuberous ligament; why they matter in delivery · also at length: nutation / counternutation, SI joint and low back pain, piriformis syndrome, Trendelenburg.",
