   "id": "n-ga-069",
   "subject": "gross-anatomy",
   "title": "Leg · III. Nerves of the Leg",
   "body": "*Key: ★ = the Leg & Knee lecture · plain bullets = Snell Ch. 10*\n\n- ★ The nerves of the leg all come from the sciatic nerve — roots L4, L5, S1, S2, S3. It goes down grouped together through the greater sciatic notch, then down the back of the thigh; in the popliteal fossa it splits into two: the tibial nerve + the common peroneal (fibular) nerve.\n- The sciatic is the largest nerve in the body — the tibial + common peroneal bound together by fascia. It gives no branches in the gluteal region; the split is at a variable site above the popliteal fossa.\n- ★ Common peroneal → goes around the neck of the fibula → superficial + deep peroneal nerves. Tibial → down the back of the leg.\n### TIBIAL NERVE\nFig 10.17 · Sciatic origin + the main branches of the tibial nerve.\n- ★ The larger of the two. Arises at the lower third of the thigh once the sciatic splits. Goes down the lateral side of the popliteal artery, crosses posterior, then runs medial — it winds around the popliteal artery (the popliteal vein lies between nerve + artery).\n- Enters the posterior compartment beneath soleus; lies on tibialis posterior, lower down on the tibia. Accompanies the posterior tibial artery (medial at first → crosses behind → lateral).\n- ★ Passes behind the medial malleolus between FDL and FHL, under the flexor retinaculum → divides into medial + lateral plantar nerves (the four layers of muscle of the sole).\n- Cutaneous: sural nerve — comes out between the two heads of gastrocnemius; follows the small saphenous vein behind the lateral malleolus → skin of the calf + lateral border of the foot + little toe; usually joined by the sural communicating branch of the common peroneal. Medial calcaneal branch → medial heel.\n- Muscular: both heads of gastrocnemius, plantaris, soleus, popliteus (+ below the fossa: soleus, FDL, FHL, tibialis posterior). Articular: knee + ankle joints.\n### COMMON PERONEAL (FIBULAR) NERVE\nFig 10.16 · Sciatic origin + the main branches of the common peroneal nerve.\n- The smaller terminal branch (lower third of the thigh). Runs along the medial border of biceps femoris, between the biceps tendon + the fibular head; crosses the lateral head of gastrocnemius → behind the head of the fibula → winds around the neck of the fibula (subcutaneous — can be rolled against the bone) → pierces peroneus longus → superficial + deep peroneal.\n- ★ The anterior group = deep peroneal; the lateral group = superficial peroneal.\n- Branches: sural communicating branch; lateral cutaneous nerve of the calf; muscular branch to the short head of biceps femoris; articular branches to the knee.\n- ★ The fibular head = the common fracture site → where the common peroneal nerve is commonly injured. If injured → foot drop: paralysis of tibialis anterior, EDL, EHL, peroneus longus + brevis and the rest of the anterior + lateral groups.\n### COMMON PERONEAL INJURY TIBIAL INJURY\nWhere exposed around the neck of the fibula — fibular-neck fractures, casts/splints, direct trauma deep + protected (beneath gastrocnemius + soleus) → rarely injured Motor anterior + lateral compartments paralyzed (TA, EDL, EDB, tertius, EHL; PL, PB) → plantar flexors + invertors unopposed → foot plantar flexed (foot drop) + inverted = equinovarus all muscles of the back of the leg + the sole paralyzed → foot dorsiflexed + everted = calcaneovalgus Sensory lost down the anterior + lateral leg, dorsum of the foot + toes (incl. medial side of the big toe); lateral foot border (sural) + medial border (saphenous) spared lost on the sole → later trophic ulcers\n### SKIN OF THE LEG — CUTANEOUS NERVES\n### AREA NERVE\nUpper lateral leg lateral cutaneous nerve of the calf (common peroneal) Lower anterolateral leg + dorsum of foot superficial peroneal (★ front of the leg + dorsum) Anteromedial + posteromedial leg saphenous nerve (femoral nerve branch) Upper back of the leg + popliteal fossa posterior cutaneous nerve of the thigh Lower posterolateral leg sural nerve (tibial; ★ joined by the sural communicating branch)",
   "order": 69,
   "updated": 1794880000000
