   "subject": "gross-anatomy",
   "title": "Lab · Abdominal Quadrants",
   "body": "*Lab practical sheet · what sits in each quadrant. R / L = the patient's right / left.*\n\n## Right upper quadrant (RUQ)\n- Liver\n- Gallbladder\n- Cystic duct, hepatic duct, common bile duct\n- Hepatic flexure\n- Portion of ascending + transverse colon\n- Portion of small intestine (duodenum)\n- Right kidney (posteriorly)\n- Pylorus of the stomach\n- Small part of the pancreas (head)\n- Portion of right ureter\n\n## Left upper quadrant (LUQ)\n- Body + cardia of the stomach\n- Portion of the esophagus\n- Spleen\n- Splenic flexure\n- Portion of descending + transverse colon\n- Portion of small intestine (jejunum)\n- Most of the pancreas (body, tail)\n- Left kidney (posteriorly)\n- Portion of left ureter\n\n## Right lower quadrant (RLQ)\n- Portion of ascending colon\n- Cecum\n- Appendix\n- Portion of small intestine (ileum)\n- Right spermatic cord\n- Right adnexa\n- Portion of right ureter\n\n## Left lower quadrant (LLQ)\n- Left portion of descending colon\n- Sigmoid colon\n- Left spermatic cord\n- Left adnexa\n- Portion of small intestine\n- Portion of left ureter",
